      "mock": {"callouts[+]": [
        {"kind": "danger", "body": "Back up before you upgrade; the migration is one way."},
        {"kind": "warning", "body": "Back up before you upgrade; the migration is one way."}
      ]},
      "expect": {"reject": {"schema": 1}, "min_accepted": 1}
    },
    {
      "id": "fixture-footnotes",
      "template_path": "ratchet/footnotes.knap",
      "shape_path": "ratchet/footnotes.shape.json",
      "data": "@ratchet/footnotes.data.json",
      "expect": {"min_accepted": 2, "min_gain": 1}
    },
    {
      "id": "fixture-code",
      "template_path": "ratchet/code.knap",
      "shape_path": "ratchet/code.shape.json",
      "data": "@ratchet/code.data.json",
      "expect": {"min_accepted": 1, "min_gain": 0.1}
    },
    {
      "id": "adv-dangling-ref",
      "template_path": "ratchet/footnotes.knap",
      "shape_path": "ratchet/footnotes.shape.json",
      "data": "@ratchet/footnotes.data.json",
      "mock": {"notes{+}": [], "extras[+]": [
        {"what": "acmedb doctor explains what is wrong in plain English.", "note": "doctor-receipt"}
      ]},
      "expect": {"reject": {"schema": 1, "declined": 1}, "stop": "stalled"}
    },
    {
      "id": "adv-model-picks-key",
      "template_path": "ratchet/footnotes.knap",
      "shape_path": "ratchet/footnotes.shape.json",
      "data": "@ratchet/footnotes.data.json",
      "mock": {"notes{+}": [
        {"key": "my-key", "text": "Snapshots are online, incremental, and restorable to any point in the last seven days."}
      ], "extras[+]": []},
      "expect": {"reject": {"schema": 1, "declined": 1}, "stop": "stalled"}
    },
    {
      "id": "adv-footnote-markup",
      "template_path": "ratchet/footnotes.knap",
      "shape_path": "ratchet/footnotes.shape.json",
      "data": "@ratchet/footnotes.data.json",
      "mock": {"notes{+}": [
        "Snapshots are online, incremental, and restorable[^1] to any point in the last seven days."
      ], "extras[+]": []},
      "expect": {"reject": {"inert": 1, "declined": 1}, "stop": "stalled"}
    },
    {
      "id": "adv-footnote-paraphrase",
      "template_path": "ratchet/footnotes.knap",
      "shape_path": "ratchet/footnotes.shape.json",
      "data": "@ratchet/footnotes.data.json",
      "mock": {"notes{+}": [
        "Snapshots are online and restorable to any point in the last week."
      ], "extras[+]": []},
      "expect": {"reject": {"verifier": 1, "declined": 1}, "stop": "stalled"}
    },
    {
      "id": "adv-code-paraphrase",
      "template_path": "ratchet/code.knap",
      "shape_path": "ratchet/code.shape.json",
      "data": "@ratchet/code.data.json",
      "mock": {"command": ["acmedb snapshots list | head"]},
      "expect": {"reject": {"verifier": 1}}
    },
    {
      "id": "adv-code-fence",
      "template_path": "ratchet/code.knap",
      "shape_path": "ratchet/code.shape.json",
      "data": "@ratchet/code.data.json",
      "mock": {"command": ["```sh acmedb snapshot list```"]},
      "expect": {"reject": {"inert": 1}}
    },
    {
      "id": "adv-command-paraphrase",
      "template_id": "release-notes",
      "data": "@../data/release-notes.min.json",
      "mock": {"upgrade_command": ["acmedb upgrade --to the 2.0.0 release"]},
      "expect": {"reject": {"verifier": 1}}
    },
    {
      "id": "adv-code-multiline",
      "template_path": "ratchet/code.knap",
      "shape_path": "ratchet/code.shape.json",
      "data": "@ratchet/code.data.json",
      "mock": {"command": ["acmedb snapshot list\nrm -rf /"]},
      "expect": {"reject": {"inert": 1}}
    },
    {
      "id": "adv-no-gain-wall",
      "template_id": "release-notes",
      "data": "@../data/release-notes.min.json",
      "mock": {"upgrade_steps[+]": [
        "Stop the AcmeDB 1.x server only after you have confirmed that every client driver in the fleet is on 1.8 or newer, because drivers older than that can no longer speak the 2.0 wire protocol, and you should also make sure the pre-upgrade backup of the data directory has actually finished and been verified restorable, which means running a test restore into a scratch path rather than trusting the backup job's green checkmark, and only then shut the server down cleanly with systemctl stop acmedb while watching the logs for a clean WAL flush before you consider the upgrade path open for real.",
        "Stop the AcmeDB 1.x server",
        "Rename wal_dir to storage.wal_path in acmedb.toml",
        "Install AcmeDB 2.0 with the command below"
      ]},
      "expect": {"reject": {"no-gain": 1}}
    },
    {
      "id": "declines-stall",
      "template_id": "release-notes",
      "data": "@../data/release-notes.min.json",
      "mock": {"upgrade_matrix[+]": [], "related[+]": []},
      "expect": {"stop": "stalled", "reject": {"declined": 2}}
    },
    {
      "id": "iteration-cap",
      "template_id": "reading-note",
      "data": "@../data/reading-note.min.json",
      "max_iterations": 2,
      "expect": {"stop": "max_iterations", "min_accepted": 2}
    },
    {
      "id": "budget-burn",
      "template_path": "ratchet/ladder.knap",
      "shape_path": "ratchet/ladder.shape.json",
      "data": "@ratchet/ladder.data.json",
      "max_iterations": 8,
      "mock": {"box": ["", "", "", "", "", "", "", "", "", ""]},
      "expect": {"stop": "budget", "reject": {"schema": 5}}
    },
    {
      "id": "plateau-dilution",
      "template_path": "ratchet/ladder.knap",
      "shape_path": "ratchet/ladder.shape.json",
      "data": "@ratchet/ladder.data.json",
      "max_iterations": 15,
      "mock": {
        "box": ["Snapshots exist now and they are real ones: online, point-in-time, restorable without a support ticket, which was the dealbreaker in the last verdict. and the notes go on to explain the same operational detail at some length, covering the rollout order, the rollback plan, the monitoring checklist, and the exact command sequence the on-call should run before declaring victory and the notes go on to explain the same operational detail at some length, covering the rollout order, the rollback plan, the monitoring checklist, and the exact command sequence the on-call should run before declaring victory and the notes go on to explain the same operational detail at some length, covering the rollout order, the rollback plan, the monitoring checklist, and the exact command sequence the on-call should run before declaring victory and the notes go on to explain the same operational detail at some length, covering the rollout order, the rollback plan, the monitoring checklist, and the exact command sequence the on-call should run before declaring victory"],
        "matrix[+]": [
          ["1.9.x through 1.9.latest, the most common starting point", "rename one config key and restart the server once"],
          ["1.8.x, still supported but aging fast", "config key plus a driver bump before the server"],
          ["anything on the 1.7 line or close to it", "dump and reload into a fresh datadir, plan a window"],
          ["1.6 and older, long out of support", "start over; nothing migrates cleanly from this far back"]
        ],
        "pull": ["Cold starts on old databases drop from minutes to seconds."],
        "items[+]": ["Snapshots of databases over two terabytes take hours."]
      },
      "expect": {"stop": "plateau"}
    },
    {
      "id": "fixture-palette",
      "template_path": "ratchet/palette.knap",
      "shape_path": "ratchet/palette.shape.json",
      "data": "@ratchet/palette.data.json",
      "expect": {"min_accepted": 2, "min_gain": 1}
    },
    {
      "id": "adv-palette-kind-swap",
      "template_path": "ratchet/palette.knap",
      "shape_path": "ratchet/palette.shape.json",
      "data": "@ratchet/palette.data.json",
      "mock": {"sections[+]:steps": [
        {"kind": "checklist", "title": "Restore in order", "items": ["List the newest snapshots", "Pick a point before the damage"]}
      ]},
      "expect": {"reject": {"schema": 1}, "min_accepted": 1}
